  VALUES ('rust', 'en', 'senior', 'What is a lifetime annotation (`''a`) and when is it needed?', '`fn longest<''a>(x: &''a str, y: &''a str) -> &''a str` — the returned reference lives at least as long as the shorter of x and y. The compiler verifies this at compile time, making dangling references impossible. Lifetime annotations are part of function signatures, not runtime behaviour.', 1, true)
  RETURNING id
)
