  VALUES ('rust', 'en', 'senior', 'When do you use `Box<T>`, `Rc<T>`, and `Arc<T>`?', '`Box<T>` moves a value to the heap — necessary for recursive types like linked lists and when you need a fixed-size pointer to unknown-size data. `Rc<T>` allows multiple owners in a single thread. `Arc<T>` is `Rc` with atomic (thread-safe) reference counting — use `Arc<Mutex<T>>` for shared mutable state across threads.', 1, true)
  RETURNING id
)
