  VALUES ('rust', 'en', 'mid', 'Why is `match` important in Rust?', '`match shape { Circle(r) => PI*r*r, Rect(w,h) => w*h }` — the compiler requires every enum variant to be covered. Adding a new variant forces all match expressions to be updated, catching missing cases at compile time. `if let` and `while let` are concise alternatives for single-pattern matching.', 1, true)
